# pulse-web-otel — contract & docs

Same npm package / folder **`pulse-web-otel/`** — this file is the **product + wiring** layer (what ships on the wire, where SPECs live, which agent/skills apply). For **how to write TS, tests, and layout**, use **`pulse-web-otel-conventions.mdc`** (narrower glob on `*.ts`/`*.tsx`).

## Rule stack (two layers, one package)

| Rule file | Globs | Role |
|-----------|-------|------|
| **`pulse-web-otel-conventions.mdc`** | `pulse-web-otel/**/*.{ts,tsx}` | Conventions — TS style, Vitest/E2E, gates, source layout + folder placement, commits |
| **`pulse-web-otel-contract.mdc`** (this file) | `pulse-web-otel/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,json}` | Contract — `platform`, `pulse.type`, public API, SPEC map, agent/skills index |

When both match a `.ts`/`.tsx` file, **conventions** win for implementation detail; **contract** still applies for telemetry/API promises.

**Legacy rule filenames (symlinks under `.cursor/rules/`):** `web-sdk.mdc` → contract; `pulse-web-otel.mdc` → conventions.

**Primary agent:** [`pulse-web-sdk.md`](../agents/pulse-web-sdk.md) — loads **web-sdk-ship**, **web-sdk-instrument**, **web-sdk-e2e-matrix** as needed. *(Cursor: `.cursor/agents/pulse-web-sdk.md` → this file; Claude Code: `.claude/agents/pulse-web-sdk.md` → this file.)*

**Skills (canonical under `.agents/skills/`; same paths symlinked as `.cursor/skills/` and `.claude/skills/`):**

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `web-sdk-ship/` | Ship-ready workflow — tests, Step 5 diff audit, doc sync |
| `web-sdk-instrument/` | Phased instrumentation (research → implementation) |
| `web-sdk-e2e-matrix/` | `DESIGN.md` / plan folder → exhaustive Playwright matrix |

